        "payload": {
          "description": "About FullStack\nFullStack is your AI-native engineering partner, built to turn AI capability into certainty. Most companies can demo AI; few can get it to production and prove what it produced. We close that gap with three capabilities, AI built into your products from the start, elite vetted talent who apply it, and transparent execution that shows value every step of the way. With now over 600 customers in North America, FullStack is one integrated partner for all your AI engineering needs. With FullStack, you move forward with confidence.\nWe’re Most Proud Of\nOffering life-changing career opportunities to talented software professionals across the Americas.\nBuilding highly-skilled software development teams for hundreds of the world’s greatest companies.\nHaving delivered hundreds of successful custom software solutions, which have positively impacted the lives and careers of millions of users.\nOur 4.1-star rating on GlassDoor.\nOur client Net Promoter Score of 68, twice the industry average.\nThe Opportunity\nJoin our talent network and connect with U.S. clients for flexible, project-based development work as an Agentic Software Engineer (Google Antigravity).\nYou will integrate directly into our client's team and work alongside their existing designers and engineers on a daily basis.\nWhat We're Looking For\n5+ years of professional software development experience with a deep understanding of full-stack architectures (e.g., Java, Python, C#, React, Node, etc.).\n1-3 years of professional experience using Google Antigravity as a primary development environment to coordinate AI-driven implementation across large, multi-file systems while maintaining architectural oversight.\nExperience delivering production software where AI systems generate the majority of implementation code.\nStrong context engineering skills, including structuring codebases, specifications, and documentation to produce reliable, context-efficient AI output.\nAbility to translate complex product requirements into machine-executable, AI-friendly specifications.\nExperience designing AI-first development workflows from specification through deployment.\nAbility to systematically improve AI-generated output through structured iteration and feedback loops.\nComfort working across multiple stacks, using AI to deliver high-quality, production-ready systems.\nExperience operating across frontend, backend, and infrastructure in AI-accelerated environments.\nDisciplined human-in-the-loop review practices, with risk-adjusted validation for high-impact or safety-critical flows.\nStrong curiosity and initiative in evaluating and adopting emerging AI-native engineering practices.\nAdvanced understanding of Agile methodologies and Lean principles and participation in team ceremonies as well as asynchronous work.\nAdvanced English is required.\nSuccessful completion of a four-year college degree is required.\nA positive mindset and a can-do attitude.\nAbility to identify with the goals of FullStack's clients and dedicate yourself to delivering on commitments.\nAbility to consistently work 40 hours per week.\nWork Authorization Requirements\nApplicants must be currently authorized to work in the country of this job posting on a full-time basis.\nFullStack will not sponsor applicants for work visas now or in the future.\nWhat We Offer\nCompetitive pay.\n100% remote work.\nThe ability to work with leading startups and Fortune 500 companies.\nContinuing education opportunities.\nOpportunity to grow and expand your career.\nOur talent network is committed to fostering a diverse, inclusive, and accessible environment where IT professionals can find opportunities that match their skills. We welcome individuals of all races, religions, genders, sexual orientations, national origins, abilities, and experiences. Our focus is on connecting talent with projects based on qualifications, ensuring a fair and transparent process that values diverse perspectives and global collaboration.\nLearn more about our Applicants Privacy Notice.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4476199697": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T13:05:12.109605+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Do you love building and pioneering in the technology space? Do you enjoy solving complex business problems in a fast-paced, collaborative, inclusive and iterative delivery environment? At Capital One, you'll be part of a big group of makers, breakers, doers and disruptors who solve real problems and meet real customer needs. We are seeking Front-end Software Engineers who are passionate about leveraging cutting-edge open source frameworks and emerging technologies. In this role, you’ll be at the forefront of driving a major transformation across Capital One.\nWhat You’ll Do:\nIncrease the reach of Capital One Shopping via SEO, AEO, and GEO\nDesign and build high-performance, highly optimized front-end code and smart front-end architectures that serve as the basis for both an amazing user experience and improved visibility in search ranking\nPartner with Software Engineers, Designers, and Product Managers to deliver high-performing, quality features for 100M+ customers that are engaging, purposeful and powerful in their simplicity\nArchitect, build, and maintain core components and shared libraries that act as a force multiplier for multiple teams within your product area\nContribute to standards for cross-platform consistency, scalability, and accessibility across front-end experiences\nServe as a subject matter expert in critical areas like SEO, web performance, networking, or design systems, influencing patterns and standards across teams\nPartner with infrastructure and backend teams to define and improve CI/CD, observability, and reliability engineering practices, standardizing release practices\nDefine strategies for leveraging agentic AI tools across multiple teams, including specialized agents, skills and tools built on open standards (e.g., Model Context Protocol), to standardize workflows\nMentor and guide senior engineers in building AI-native workflows, shaping the next generation of technical leaders proficient in agentic coding\nApply mastery of the modern web ecosystem (including PWAs, Wasm, mobile web, and Service Workers) to make complex, high-leverage, hands-on technical contributions that solve the most challenging problems within your product area\nBasic Qualifications:\nBachelor's Degree or higher in Computer Science or a related quantitative field (Statistics, Economics, Operations Research, Analytics, Mathematics, Engineering)\nAt least 6 years of professional experience in software engineering (internship experience does not apply)\nAt least 6 years of experience developing applications using TypeScript, HTML, CSS and modern web frameworks (React, Angular, Vue, Svelte)\nAt least 3 years of experience architecting or leading the development of federated front-end or design systems with cross-application adoption\nPreferred Qualifications:\n7+ years of experience with TypeScript and JavaScript\n7+ years of experience with modern web frameworks (e.g., React, Angular, Vue, Svelte), HTML and CSS\nProven experience with automated testing frameworks (e.g., Jest, Cypress, Playwright) and modular architecture\nAdept at navigating the ever-shifting world of SEO - a deep understanding of how to improve search rankings\nExperience leading the design of multi-team components or contributing to shared design systems\nExpertise in release health indicators, metrics-driven canary release, and feature flag strategies\nExpertise with agentic AI coding tools and developer productivity patterns\nExposure to micro-frontend patterns and practices, along with an understanding of where they add value vs increase overhead\nCapital One will consider sponsoring a new qualified applicant for employment authorization for this position.\nThe minimum and maximum full-time annual salaries for this role are listed below, by location. Please note that this salary information is solely for candidates hired to perform work within one of these locations, and refers to the amount Capital One is willing to pay at the time of this posting. Salaries for part-time roles will be prorated based upon the agreed upon number of hours to be regularly worked.\nRemote (Regardless of Location): $209,000 - $238,500 for Front-end Engineer 5\nMcLean, VA: $229,900 - $262,400 for Front-end Engineer 5\nCandidates hired to work in other locations will be subject to the pay range associated with that location, and the actual annualized salary amount offered to any candidate at the time of hire will be reflected solely in the candidate’s offer letter.\nThis role is also eligible to earn performance based incentive compensation, which may include cash bonus(es) and/or long term incentives (LTI). Incentives could be discretionary or non discretionary depending on the plan.\nCapital One offers a comprehensive, competitive, and inclusive set of health, financial and other benefits that support your total well-being. Learn more at the Capital One Careers website. Eligibility varies based on full or part-time status, exempt or non-exempt status, and management level.\nThis role is expected to accept applications for a minimum of 5 business days.\nNo agencies please. Capital One is an equal opportunity employer (EOE, including disability/vet) committed to non-discrimination in compliance with applicable federal, state, and local laws. Capital One promotes a drug-free workplace. Capital One will consider for employment qualified applicants with a criminal history in a manner consistent with the requirements of applicable laws regarding criminal background inquiries, including, to the extent applicable, Article 23-A of the New York Correction Law; San Francisco, California Police Code Article 49, Sections 4901-4920; New York City’s Fair Chance Act; Philadelphia’s Fair Criminal Records Screening Act; and other applicable federal, state, and local laws and regulations regarding criminal background inquiries.\nIf you have visited our website in search of information on employment opportunities or to apply for a position, and you require an accommodation, please contact Capital One Recruiting at 1-800-304-9102 or via email at RecruitingAccommodation@capitalone.com. All information you provide will be kept confidential and will be used only to the extent required to provide needed reasonable accommodations.\nFor technical support or questions about Capital One's recruiting process, please send an email to Careers@capitalone.com\nCapital One does not provide, endorse nor guarantee and is not liable for third-party products, services, educational tools or other information available through this site.\nCapital One Financial is made up of several different entities. Please note that any position posted in Canada is for Capital One Canada, any position posted in the United Kingdom is for Capital One Europe and any position posted in the Philippines is for Capital One Philippines Service Corp. (COPSSC).",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4481398581": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T13:05:12.109605+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Most companies treat support as a cost center. We treat it as an engineering challenge and a product opportunity.\nSupport Operations Engineering is an engineering function inside ClickHouse’s Support Services organization. We build the systems that decide how customers get help from the moment they describe their problem to the moment it’s resolved. This role will help shape how Support Services, RevOps, GTM, and core Engineering teams collaborate on customers. This is not a tools team. About a third of our work directly supports the support organization. The rest is building experiences and systems that change how ClickHouse works with its customers in more effective, streamlined ways.\nWhat you will be doing\nYou’ll Design And Build The Systems That Sit Between ClickHouse’s Customers And The Teams Who Serve Them. The Work Is Varied By Design, And You’ll Move Between Problem Types As Priorities Shift\nIntelligent routing and decision systems. Software that decides where work should go and who should handle it, weighing many signals at once, and is built to adapt as the business scales.\nAI-powered customer experiences. Customer-facing and internal experiences that understand what someone needs, recommend the best next step, and know when to hand off to a human.\nInternal platforms and tooling. Applications that give Support, RevOps, and GTM teams the leverage to work faster and more accurately, built to production standards.\nIntegrations and data flow. Connections across Salesforce, live chat, incident management, Slack, GitHub, and more, so workflows and data move cleanly between systems.\nAutomation and observability. Systems that remove repetitive work, surface what’s breaking, and give teams confidence in what they’re running.\nAcross all of it, you’ll partner with core Engineering to ship to production, and own what you build: code review, testing, monitoring, and continuous improvement.\nWhat You Bring Along\n3–5 years building and shipping full-stack software in production, with tools like TypeScript/JavaScript, Node.js, and React (or comparable)\nExperience developing with APIs, webhooks, and integrations between distributed systems\nHands-on experience close to support: as a support or technical support engineer, or by building tools or integrations for a support, CS, or RevOps team\nConfidence with Git and safe, version-controlled deployment workflows\nThe ability to translate operational needs into solutions that non-engineers can follow\nA shipper’s mindset: self-driven, curious, and comfortable owning a problem end-to-end in a remote, globally distributed team\nComfort using AI tools day to day in how you build, with a clear sense of where to trust them\nBonus Points\nExperience building LLM-powered features in production (routing, retrieval, evaluation, or observability)\nSalesforce platform experience (Apex, LWC, Flows, custom objects) or certifications; if you don’t have it, the appetite to get there quickly\nSupport and incident tooling: Pylon, incident.io, PagerDuty, Zendesk, Slack APIs, GitHub APIs\nExperience with ClickHouse or other analytical databases\nExperience in an early-stage or greenfield environment, or embedded in a support, RevOps, or business-systems function\nPerks\nFlexible work environment - ClickHouse is a globally distributed company and remote-friendly. We currently operate in over 25 countries.\nHealthcare - Employer contributions towards your healthcare.\nEquity in the company - Every new team member who joins our company receives stock options.\nTime off - Flexible time off in the US, generous entitlement in other countries.\nA USD$500 Home office setup if you’re a remote employee.\nGlobal Gatherings – We believe in the power of in-person connection and offer opportunities to engage with colleagues at company-wide offsites.\nCulture - We All Shape It\nAs part of a rapidly scaling start-up, you will be instrumental in shaping our culture.\nAre you interested in finding out more about our culture? Learn more about our values here. Check out our blog posts or follow us on LinkedIn to find out more about what’s happening at ClickHouse.\nEqual Opportunity & Privacy\nClickHouse provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type based on factors such as race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws.\nPlease see here for our Privacy Statement.\nCompensation Range: $154K - $215K",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4481422146": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T13:05:12.109605+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Full Stack AI Developer | Python, React & Automation\nRemote – India or Pakistan | Full-Time\nSalary: $2,000 USD per month (flexible for exceptional talent)\nExperience: 3–5 years preferred | Ability matters more than years\nHelp us build an AI-powered recruitment company.\nAt We Are Revolution , we're building something ambitious: a recruitment business where AI, intelligent automation and great technology power almost everything we do.\nWe operate across the US and European recruitment markets, and we're investing heavily in technology to transform how our business works.\nOur goal is to automate entire workflows — from finding candidates and identifying opportunities to matching jobs, communicating with clients, managing recruitment pipelines and analysing performance.\nWe're looking for a talented Full Stack Developer who loves building things, solving problems and using AI to work faster and smarter.\nYou'll join a small, ambitious engineering team, working closely with our Head of Engineering to turn ideas into working products.\nThis isn't a role where you'll spend your days fixing tickets or making minor changes to somebody else's software.\nYou'll be building real systems, solving real business problems and seeing your work used every day.\nWhat you'll be building\nYou'll work across a variety of exciting projects, including:\nAI Agents: Building intelligent agents using Claude, OpenAI and other AI tools to automate complex business processes.\nFull Stack Applications: Developing internal platforms, dashboards and applications using React, Next.js, Python and FastAPI.\nBusiness Automation: Creating workflows using n8n, Python, APIs and AI to eliminate repetitive manual tasks.\nIntelligent Data Systems: Connecting and organising large volumes of candidate, client and recruitment data.\nSystem Integrations: Connecting Salesforce, recruitment CRMs, email platforms, calling systems and third-party APIs.\nAI-Powered Recruitment Tools: Developing systems that identify opportunities, match candidates to jobs and recommend the next best action.\nInfrastructure & Deployment: Deploying and maintaining reliable, scalable applications using modern cloud platforms.\nYou'll have the opportunity to work on projects from initial idea through to development, deployment and continuous improvement.\nThe skills we're looking for\nEssential:\nStrong experience with Python and JavaScript/TypeScript.\nExperience building full stack applications using React or Next.js.\nExperience developing APIs and backend services, ideally using FastAPI.\nGood understanding of databases, SQL and data structures.\nExperience integrating third-party APIs.\nExperience building automations using n8n, Python or similar tools.\nConfident using AI coding tools such as Claude Code, Cursor or GitHub Copilot.\nAbility to independently solve problems and deliver working software.\nNice to have:\nSupabase or Firebase.\nRender, Railway or similar deployment platforms.\nAI agents, MCP, LLM APIs or agent orchestration.\nSalesforce integrations.\nExperience building data pipelines or large-scale automation systems.\nYou don't need to know every technology listed. We're much more interested in someone who can learn quickly, solve problems and build great software.\nThe type of person who will thrive here\nWe're looking for a genuine builder.\nSomeone who enjoys taking a problem, understanding what needs to happen and figuring out the best way to make it work.\nYou'll probably enjoy this role if you:\nLove coding and building new products.\nAlready use AI tools to make yourself a more productive developer.\nEnjoy learning new technologies and experimenting with new ideas.\nTake ownership rather than waiting for detailed instructions.\nCan work across frontend, backend, databases and automation.\nCare about delivering working solutions, not just writing code.\nCommunicate clearly and enjoy being part of a collaborative team.\nWe value intelligence, curiosity, speed of learning and execution more than impressive CVs or academic qualifications.\nWhy join We Are Revolution?\nBuild with AI every day. You'll work with modern AI tools, automation platforms and emerging technologies on genuine commercial applications.\nWork on meaningful projects. Your software won't sit unused. You'll see the impact of what you build across a growing international business.\nReal responsibility and ownership. You'll be trusted to contribute ideas, make technical decisions and own projects.\nWork alongside experienced leadership. You'll collaborate directly with our Head of Engineering and company leadership, who are committed to investing in technology.\nOpportunity to grow. We're building an increasingly sophisticated technology platform, creating opportunities to develop your skills and responsibilities as the team grows.\nRemote working. Work from India or Pakistan as part of an international team.\nCompetitive compensation. We're looking for capability, not simply the cheapest developer. We'll consider stronger packages for exceptional candidates.\nHow to apply\nWe'd love to hear from you if you're a developer who genuinely enjoys building things and wants to work at the intersection of AI, software engineering and business automation .\nPlease send us your CV, GitHub or portfolio, and tell us briefly:\nWhat's the most interesting application, AI agent or automation you've personally built, and what did it achieve?\nWe care much more about what you've actually built than how many technologies you can list on your CV.\nCome and help us build the future of AI-powered recruitment.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4481445030": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T13:05:12.109605+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About the role:\nWe’re looking for a software engineer who is also interested in crypto markets and comfortable participating in day trading as part of the role.\nYou’ll work with us to research trading strategies, analyze market data, and build algorithms that can be tested and improved over time. A major part of the work will be studying 10 years or more of historical data where available , identifying patterns, testing hypotheses, and using evidence to evaluate trading ideas.\nThis is one integrated role: you’ll contribute to both the trading work and the software behind it. We’re open to students, recent graduates, and experienced candidates who can show strong technical and analytical skills alongside genuine crypto trading experience.\nWe value practical problem-solving. You should be comfortable finding useful exchanges, APIs, datasets, libraries, open-source projects, and existing tools, then connecting them into a working system. The goal is to build a stable crypto trading algorithm by assembling and improving what already works—not rebuilding every component from scratch.\nWhat you’ll do\nParticipate in crypto market research and day-trading activity.\nAnalyze long-term historical market data, including 10 years or more where reliable data is available.\nCollect, clean, validate, and analyze data from crypto exchanges and other relevant sources.\nUse data analysis and critical thinking to identify patterns, test hypotheses, and assess whether a strategy has evidence behind it.\nStudy price action, market behavior, and trading strategies, and help translate useful ideas into testable rules.\nDevelop Python tools and services for data collection, analysis, and automation.\nWork with exchange APIs, libraries, and other data sources; use scripting or automation where appropriate.\nResearch technical indicators and formulas using reliable references, open-source tools, and AI assistants such as Claude.\nVerify formulas and AI-generated code before using them in analysis or trading systems.\nConnect existing tools and services to fill gaps in the trading workflow.\nBuild and improve backtesting, monitoring, alerting, and execution components.\nTest strategies with historical data and simulated trading, then help evaluate live trading under defined risk limits.\nDocument your methods, assumptions, results, and limitations so the team can make data-informed decisions.\nWhat we’re looking for\nStrong interest in cryptocurrency markets and demonstrable experience buying, selling, or day trading crypto.\nComfort participating in day-trading research and activity as well as software development.\nStrong data analysis and critical analysis skills, with the ability to question assumptions and interpret results carefully.\nWorking knowledge of Python, including writing scripts for data collection, analysis, and automation.\nExperience using APIs, preferably exchange APIs, and handling structured data such as JSON.\nAbility to work with historical and time-series data and to evaluate trading ideas using evidence.\nFamiliarity with appropriate tools for data-driven analysis, such as pandas, NumPy, SQL, notebooks, statistical methods, or visualization tools.\nAbility to research indicators, understand the logic behind them, and translate ideas into code.\nA practical mindset: you look for suitable existing tools and libraries before building a replacement.\nGood communication skills and the ability to explain your reasoning, trading ideas, and technical decisions.\nCuriosity, discipline, and a willingness to learn from experiments that do not produce the expected result.\nHelpful experience\nFamiliarity with crypto exchanges, market-data feeds, order types, and trading dashboards.\nExperience analyzing large datasets, historical price data, or time-series data.\nExposure to backtesting, quantitative analysis, algorithmic trading, or risk management.\nExperience with tools such as Cursor, Claude, or other AI coding assistants.\nContributions to relevant open-source projects or personal trading, data analysis, or software projects.\nWho should apply\nYou do not need a particular degree or a long employment history. Students, recent graduates, self-taught developers, and experienced professionals are all welcome to apply if they can demonstrate relevant skills and trading experience.\nThis role combines hands-on crypto market participation with software engineering and data analysis. If you are interested only in coding and are not comfortable engaging with day-trading activity, this role may not be the right fit.\nHow to apply\nPlease include your résumé or LinkedIn profile.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4481891876": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T13:05:12.109605+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This position offers a leadership role in designing and building scalable full stack systems, encompassing backend services, data models, and frontend architectures that support complex, data-driven product experiences. The candidate will operate as a hands-on technical leader, influencing core services and delivering end-to-end applications that leverage AI capabilities for enterprise insight and operational efficiency.\nKey Responsibilities\nLead the design, development, and deployment of full stack applications, including backend services, APIs (REST/GraphQL), and frontend interfaces, ensuring modularity, security, and high performance.\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams—Product, Design, Data Science—to translate requirements into intuitive, reliable user experiences and scalable backend solutions.\nDefine and evolve canonical data models, manage complex entity relationships (graphs, hierarchies), and develop indexing/search solutions (Elasticsearch, vector search) supporting AI-driven search and recommendation features.\nBuild event-driven architectures (Kafka, cloud pub/sub), implementing asynchronous workflows and stream processing for scalable, real-time data handling.\nIntegrate AI/ML functionalities—such as retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), semantic search, and entity resolution—into workflows, optimizing usability and business impact.\nEstablish frontend architecture using modern frameworks (React, Vue, Angular) with focus on performance, accessibility, and shared UI component libraries.\nDrive service reliability, system observability, automated testing, and continuous improvement practices.\nImplement robust security measures, including role-based (RBAC) and attribute-based access controls (ABAC), across all layers of the application stack.\nMentor engineering teams in architecture, code quality, and technical innovation, fostering best practices and engineering excellence.\nCoordinate with DevOps and Security to ensure compliant, scalable, and resilient infrastructure, primarily on cloud platforms like AWS.\nCore Qualifications & Requirements\n5+ years of professional full stack software engineering, with demonstrated leadership in complex enterprise systems.\nStrong expertise in backend frameworks (FastAPI, Django) and frontend frameworks (React, Vue, Angular) with modern build tools (Vite).\nProficiency in Python and TypeScript; solid understanding of data modeling (relational, NoSQL, graph databases).\nExtensive experience designing and consuming RESTful and GraphQL APIs, with large-scale, service-oriented architecture knowledge.\nHands-on experience with event-driven systems (Kafka, cloud pub/sub) and asynchronous processing pipelines.\nSkilled in implementing security controls (RBAC, ABAC) and multi-tenant applications, with familiarity in search technologies (Elasticsearch, vector search).\nDeep understanding of cloud-native development in AWS; CI/CD, observability, and automation practices.\nFamiliarity with AI/ML feature integration, including retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), semantic search, and AI workflow observability.\nAbility to translate technical solutions into scalable, business-oriented products and collaborate across multidisciplinary teams.\nNice-to-Have Qualifications\nAdvanced degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or related fields; relevant cloud certifications (AWS, Azure, GCP).\nExperience in data-intensive industries such as finance, property management, or enterprise analytics.\nActive use of AI coding assistants and agents, with an understanding of their application in modern software development workflows.\nKnowledge of search optimization and domain-specific data modeling within complex enterprise environments.\nCore Technical Skills\nBackend: Python, FastAPI, Django\nFrontend: React, Vue, Angular, Vite, JavaScript/TypeScript\nAPIs: REST, GraphQL\nDatabases: Relational (PostgreSQL, MySQL), NoSQL, Graph databases\nEvent systems: Kafka, cloud pub/sub (AWS SNS/SQS)\nSearch: Elasticsearch, vector search, retrieval systems\nCloud: AWS (S3, EC2, Lambda, CloudWatch)\nAI/ML: Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), semantic search, entity resolution, AI integrations\nSecurity: RBAC, ABAC, multi-tenancy\nDevOps: CI/CD pipelines, observability, automation\nCareer Impact\nJoin a forward-thinking organization driving innovation in knowledge automation through AI, where your leadership will directly influence the development of impactful enterprise solutions.\nCompensation and Benefits\n$200,000-$240,000, comprehensive benefits package, and flexible remote work options aligned with EST working hours. Occasional travel (2-3 times per year) is expected.\nApply Today!\nTake the next step in your career by contributing to a pioneering AI-driven platform with a dynamic team of industry leaders.\nThe Phoenix Group Advisors is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace and prohibit discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, or veteran status. We strive to attract talented individuals from all backgrounds and provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482718175": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T13:05:12.109605+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About Contour\nContour Software has grown from a dozen people to over 2,000 staff across 3 cities, in less than 14 years.\nAs a subsidiary of Constellation Software Inc., we are proud to be part of a global enterprise software conglomerate that has grown to become one of the top 10 software companies in the world, with employees and customers in 100+ countries. With a broad-based and ever-growing portfolio of market-leading, vertical-market enterprise solutions covering more than 100 industry domains in predominantly mature markets, CSI's recipe creates the perfect environment for professionals to build fulfilling, long-term careers.\nWhat started as an R&D & Accounting back-office, has progressed into a full-service Global Centre serving all functions and departments, at the divisional as well as operating group/corporate level. Today Contour employees, located in Karachi, Lahore & Islamabad, are serving CSI divisions located in time zones spanning the globe, from Sydney to Vancouver. With the global growth of Constellation as the wind in our sails, we are only just getting started!\nThe Division\nJonas Premier Construction - a division of Constellation Software Inc. – is the market-leading cloud-based integrated construction management solution, for mid-sized General Contractors, Design Builders and Land Developers. Constellation companies are leading developers of technology solutions for vertical markets in North America, Europe and Australia. Jonas Software is the valued technology partner of over 8000 customers worldwide in 15 countries. Jonas is headquartered in Canada and also operates offices in the United States, the United Kingdom, and the Caribbean.\nThe Position\nWe are looking for Trainee Software Developers to join one of our R&D teams. The selected candidates will be trained for 3 to 3.5 months to become good developers capable of working on enterprise-level applications. After the end of the internship period, there is a good possibility of full-time employment based on satisfactory performance during the internship.\nThe chosen individuals will work out of the Contour Software Lahore resource center office, as an extension of the division-based R&D department.\nRequired Qualifications & Skills\nBS/MS in Computer Science or related field.\nStrong understanding of object-oriented programming principles.\nGood programming concepts and knowledge of .NET programming\nExposure to Generative AI, LLMs, RAG, Prompt Engineering, or AI-powered application development.\nStrong competencies in data structures, algorithms, and software design.\nStrong relational database concepts with SQL queries.\nGood level of knowledge of REST APIs.\nExperience and knowledge of Git.\nA quick learner, with attention to detail, and a commitment to meet deadlines.\nKnowledge of professional software engineering practices\nGood programming concepts and knowledge of frontend programming with JavaScript, AngularJS/Angular.\nGood communication skills in English.\nDisclaimer: At Contour, we attribute our success to the unique contributions of our diverse staff. We’re committed to fostering a culture of respect that thrives on the varied perspectives and experiences of all individuals we recruit, employ, promote, and compensate. Since day one, we’ve adhered to a policy that champions a work environment honoring the worth and dignity of each person while being free from all forms of employment discrimination.\nIn our continuous effort to promote inclusivity, we extend our commitment to individuals with special needs by providing reasonable accommodations. We actively encourage qualified individuals with special needs to apply for the various openings within our company. Should you require assistance in completing the application process or have any inquiries regarding special facilities, please do not hesitate to contact our HR team. Your unique talents and abilities are welcomed and valued here.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483527878": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T13:05:12.109605+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Objective\nYour role as Software Engineer is to independently design, develop, test, and maintain full-stack software solutions across backend and frontend layers. You will own assigned features from requirement analysis through implementation, integration, QA handover, and production support, while ensuring solutions are reliable, maintainable, secure, and aligned with established engineering standards.\nMain Tasks\nDesign, develop, and maintain backend services, APIs, business logic, data processing, frontend applications, dashboards, portals, forms, reporting screens, internal tools, and reusable components.\nOwn assigned features from requirement analysis through development, testing support, QA handover, defect resolution, and production support, with limited supervision.\nImplement complete end-to-end features covering frontend user interactions, backend processing, PostgreSQL data persistence, event queue processing, integrations, and final user or system responses.\nDesign and consume REST APIs, including request and response models, validations, authentication, authorization, error handling, and appropriate integration behavior.\nImplement and maintain integration flows with internal services, operators, aggregators, third-party systems, callbacks, and webhooks, ensuring proper error handling and operational visibility.\nDevelop and validate PostgreSQL queries and database interactions, including transaction behavior, indexing, constraints, data persistence, and consistency requirements for assigned features.\nImplement and support RabbitMQ and event-driven workflows, including event publishing, message consumption, payload validation, retries, dead-letter handling awareness, logging, and queue-processing monitoring.\nImplement and support asynchronous workflows such as notifications, billing triggers, delivery reports, background jobs, audit events, and integration callbacks according to system requirements.\nAnalyze business and technical requirements, identify implementation gaps and dependencies, and propose appropriate technical approaches for assigned features before development.\nTroubleshoot and resolve technical issues across backend services, APIs, frontend behavior, PostgreSQL results, event queues, integrations, asynchronous processes, and end-to-end application flows.\nPerform unit testing, support integration and regression testing, resolve identified defects, and validate implemented changes before QA handover and release.\nOptimize standard application performance, including API response times, frontend rendering behavior, PostgreSQL queries, database interactions, and event-processing efficiency.\nCollaborate with QA, Product, DevOps, Support, Security, and other engineering teams to resolve dependencies and ensure smooth end-to-end delivery.\nProvide basic technical guidance to Junior Software Engineers when required and support them in resolving straightforward development and troubleshooting issues.\nEscalate complex architectural, scalability, security, performance, event-driven design, and production-critical concerns to Senior or Lead Software Engineers when required.\nMaintain technical documentation covering APIs, integrations, frontend components, database interactions, event flows, application workflows, configurations, and known technical limitations.\nEnsure development activities comply with Jira traceability, Git and branching practices, pull request and code review requirements, SonarQube validation, secure coding, documentation, and release standards.\nQualifications\nBachelor’s degree in computer science, Software Engineering, Computer Engineering, Information Technology, or a related field.\n2+ years of experience in software development across backend and frontend applications.\nHands-on experience developing and integrating APIs, databases, and full-stack application features.\nExperience with database-driven applications, event-driven or asynchronous processing, and system integrations.\nExposure to messaging, real-time, high-volume, or integration-heavy platforms is considered an advantage.\nProfessional proficiency in Local Language and English is required.\nGood hands-on knowledge of backend development using Java or C#.NET and frontend development using React and Next.js.\nGood understanding of REST APIs, authentication, authorization, integration patterns, callbacks, webhooks, and error handling.\nGood knowledge of PostgreSQL, SQL queries, transactions, indexing fundamentals, constraints, data persistence, and validation.\nGood understanding of RabbitMQ or similar event-queuing technologies, including producers, consumers, message handling, retries, dead-letter concepts, and asynchronous processing.\nAbility to independently develop and troubleshoot complete features across backend, frontend, database, integration, and event-processing layers.\nGood knowledge of Git workflows, branching strategies, pull requests, code reviews, and development traceability.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483668874": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T13:05:12.109605+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Req197061\nPosition Purpose\nThe Software Engineer is responsible for assisting in developing and designing a product that Home Depot customers and associates will love. As a Software Engineer, you will be part of a dynamic team with engineers of all experience levels who help each other build and grow technical and leadership skills while creating, deploying, and supporting production applications. In addition, Software Engineers may be involved in product configuration, security, resilience, performance tuning and production monitoring.\nKey Responsibilities\n60% Delivers and Executes - Assists in developing, testing, deploying, and maintaining software; Follows best practices established by the organization and participates in improvement conversations; Consistently helps the team achieve results, even under tough circumstances\n20% Learns and Grows - Learns through successful and failed experiment when tackling new problems; Actively seeks ways to grow and be challenged using both formal and informal development channels\n20% Plans and Aligns - Builds partnerships and works collaboratively with others to meet shared objectives; Collaborates with other team members in agile processes; Relates openly and comfortably with diverse groups of people\nDirect Manager/Direct Reports\nThis position typically reports to Software Engineer Manager or Sr. Manager\nThis position has 0 Direct Reports\nTravel Requirements\nNo travel required.\nPhysical Requirements\nMost of the time is spent sitting in a comfortable position and there is frequent opportunity to move about. On rare occasions there may be a need to move or lift light articles.\nWorking Conditions\nLocated in a comfortable indoor area. Any unpleasant conditions would be infrequent and not objectionable.\nMinimum Qualifications\nMust be eighteen years of age or older.\nMust be legally permitted to work in the United States.\nPreferred Qualifications\n1–3 years of relevant work experience\nExperience in an object-oriented programming language (preferably Java)\nExperience with event-driven architectures and message queuing/streaming platforms (specifically Google Cloud Pub/Sub)\nExperience with NoSQL database systems, particularly Apache Cassandra, in high-throughput environments\nExperience querying, analyzing, and working with large datasets using BigQuery (BQ) or relational databases (SQL)\nHands-on experience building, managing, and maintaining observability, metrics, and alerting systems using Prometheus and Grafana\nExperience or familiarity leveraging modern AI developer tools (e.g., Claude, LLM-based coding assistants) to augment development workflows, code reviews, and problem-solving\nExperience in microservice-based architecture and cloud computing techniques (GCP preferred)\nExperience in CI/CD tools and automated deployment pipelines\nExperience in source code version control (e.g., Git)\nExperience with modern debugging and root cause analysis techniques\nExposure to security frameworks for user and service authorization and authentication\nExposure to creating and executing unit, functional, destructive, and performance tests\nMinimum Education\nThe knowledge, skills and abilities typically acquired through the completion of a bachelor's degree program or equivalent degree in a field of study related to the job.\nPreferred Education\nNo additional education\nMinimum Years Of Work Experience\n1\nPreferred Years Of Work Experience\nNo additional years of experience\nMinimum Leadership Experience\nNone\nPreferred Leadership Experience\nNone\nCertifications\nNone\nCompetencies\nGlobal Perspective\nManages Ambiguity\nNimble Learning\nSelf-Development\nCollaborates\nCultivates Innovation\nSituational Adaptability\nCommunicates Effectively\nDrives Results\nInterpersonal Savvy",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483695037": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T13:05:12.109605+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Intelligems builds the AI agents that turn your traffic into profit. Every day, brands makes thousands of decisions — what to show, what to offer, how to price for each visitor — and most of them happen by default. We build the data and the agents that make those decisions for you, automatically, so your site gets smarter with every visitor instead of sitting static. Our mission is to make every one of those decisions intelligent: grounded in what actually works, not guesswork.\nWe have excellent traction: we’re working with over 3,000 brands and have access to more than $10B of transaction and shopping session data. We are looking for highly talented individuals to join us and help us continue to scale efficiently. We have an extremely high-performing team, with a collaborative culture of low-ego + high-IQ people. Our people are our strongest asset, and we hold a very high bar.\nWe're backed by Stage 2 Ventures, Vinyl Capital, Matchstick Ventures, Techstars, and the founders of companies like Klaviyo and Postscript, and have raised >$11M to date.\nThe Role\nRoll up your sleeves and let’s build together! From day one, we’ll ask you to contribute to any and every aspect of our stack. It could be adding new functionality to the core experimentation capabilities of the platform, designing and implementing a new integration, or reworking a complicated user flow.\nOur team is lean and mean — less than 10 engineers and only a handful of product and design. This means you’ll work closely with everyone, including those in non-technical roles like our sales, support, and success teams.\nMonth one will be characterized by “learning by doing” - taking on features that are meaningful in impact with input from other teammates to get deep in the codebase and concepts while also providing value to our customers.\nFrom there you’ll tackle increasingly complex and ambiguous problems. With varying degrees of input from your product and design teammates, you’ll figure out the implementation details from schema and API design to UI polish.\nWe have thousands of customers, too, so there are often opportunities to work directly or indirectly with them. Understanding the customer perspective and having empathy are important skills that will help make you effective in each of the countless micro design decisions you make each day.\nTech Stack\nKnowledge in all of these is not required, but you should be excited to work within and help us improve the stack.\nTypeScript monorepo\nFrontend - React web app hosted on AWS S3/Cloudfront; Redux, Material UI, ReactQuery\nBackend - Serverless NodeJS hosted on AWS Lambda, managed by SST. MySQL database. Also includes SQS queues, Dynamo tables, dockerized lambdas, etc….\n“Plugin” - Compiled client-side javascript written in Typescript\nAnalytics - AWS Eventbus, Kinesis, Flink, Kafka, and Clickhouse.\nYou’re a Great Fit If\nYou have experience owning product and feature development from ideation to delivery\nYou’re able to hold a lot of context in your head — there are a lot of moving pieces here to keep in mind\nExploration, learning, and experimentation are core to your process\nYou have deep expertise in areas that will level us up\nAt the same time have curiosity to learn try a different approach\nYou empathize with our customers, and care deeply about making them successful\nYou're a team player and can work collaboratively while also being independent\nYou want to shape the future of e-commerce\nNote: please only apply to ONE software engineering role at Intelligems. We are able to move candidates between the Frontend & Full Stack roles as needed.\nBenefits for full-time employees:\nCompetitive salary and equity packages\nMedical, dental, and vision insurance (varies by country)\n401k + match (U.S. only)\nFlexible PTO policy\nParental leave\n$ to spend quarterly with our growing list of brands\nWFH setup stipend\nLaptop provided\nTeam meetups and events\nBenefits & perks may vary outside of the U.S.\nIntelligems is a remote-first company with 4 offices (NYC, Denver, Boston, and Chicago), but please note that some travel may be required.\nAll Intelligems interviews are transcribed by an AI notetaker.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484040948": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T13:05:12.109605+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Purpose\nWe are looking for a highly skilled Java Developer with strong experience in Spring Boot and Microservices architecture. The ideal candidate will design, develop, and maintain scalable backend services in a cloud-native environment.\nKey Result Areas\n• Design and develop RESTful APIs using Java 8/11/17\n• Build microservices using Spring Boot\n• Implement service-to-service communication (REST, Kafka, etc.)\n• Work with relational and NoSQL databases\n• Write clean, testable, production-grade code\n• Participate in architecture discussions and technical design\n• Implement security using JWT/OAuth2\n• Optimize application performance and scalability\n• Follow CI/CD and DevOps practices\n• Troubleshoot production issues and perform root cause analysis\nKnowledge, Skills and Experience\n• Strong experience in Java & OOP concepts\n• Hands-on experience with Spring Boot\n• Experience building Microservices architecture\n• Experience with REST APIs\n• Database experience (SQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle, MongoDB)\n• Understanding of Docker & Kubernetes\nExperience with Git\n• Familiarity with CI/CD pipelines",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-10-28T13:05:12.109605+00:00"
  },
  "cache:posts": {
    "entries": {
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/alhazan-mubarak_fintech-nigeria-cloudcomputing-share-7516453508934422528-06Zm": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T13:06:47.708354+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "I assumed AWS Local Zone in Lagos was the easy answer to the CBN localisation requirement. Then I sat down and read the documentation properly.\n\nIt isn't, at least not for the data layer.\n\nThere's no RDS in the Lagos Local Zone, so you'd be self-managing Postgres or MySQL on EC2. Also, Local Zones extend a parent Region (Lagos is linked to af-south-1), so EBS snapshots write to S3 in the parent Region by default. Local snapshots only work in Local Zones with S3 in-zone, and Lagos doesn't have that. So your backups end up in Cape Town.\n\nWhich leads to the bigger problem. There's no AWS Region in Nigeria. No Azure Region or Google Cloud Region either. If your payment database runs on a hyperscaler today, it's sitting in Ireland, Virginia or Cape Town — and so are your automated backups and your KMS keys.\n\nThe June circular requires payment transaction data generated in Nigeria to be stored and managed in Nigeria from 1 January 2027. That's under 90 days. For most teams, this isn't a settings change, because there's nowhere to point it at.\n\nThe harder question is what \"𝐬𝐭𝐨𝐫𝐞𝐝 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐦𝐚𝐧𝐚𝐠𝐞𝐝 𝐢𝐧 𝐍𝐢𝐠𝐞𝐫𝐢𝐚\" actually means in practice. Several law firms read it as covering the primary processing environment rather than just a copy held locally, which would mean backing up from a hyperscaler into Nigeria doesn't meet it. I put that question to Huawei Cloud directly and got the same answer, though they'd obviously have an interest in saying so.\n\nI've been working out how Nigerian startups can meet these requirements without needing a large infrastructure team or building everything from scratch.\n\nIf you're working through this at a Nigerian fintech or building infrastructure for one, I'd be glad to compare notes.\n\n#Fintech #Nigeria #CloudComputing #AWS",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-15T11:02:45.655Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/china-produces-about-85-of-the-worlds-cathode-share-7516513337908633600-8_eD": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T13:06:47.708354+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "China produces about 85% of the world's cathode active material. The West needs new battery chemistries to compete, but traditional R&D can take years to deliver them. \n \nToday, we announced $45M in funding to change that. \n \nBacked by  Zone II Ventures, and Course Corrected, we're scaling our AI-powered Discovery Engine, which combines 18 years of proprietary battery data with automated labs that physically build and test new materials. Over these 18 years our platform has run more than 225 projects for more than 85 customers across the battery value chain, including nearly a dozen Fortune 500 companies, and has resulted in more than 100 battery patents.  Along the way, the platform generated an internally consistent dataset covering more than 500,000 physical cells tested at over 165 million cycles.  \n \nOur technology has already helped deliver DRX, a new family of nickel- and cobalt-free cathode materials designed to reduce dependence on China. Now, we're bringing DRX toward commercialization while using AI to accelerate the next generation of breakthroughs. \n \nLed by founder and CEO Mathias Ingvarsson, COO and former Tesla manufacturing leader Steven Prast, and Chief Scientific Officer Dee Strand, we're building a faster path from battery discovery to commercial deployment. \n \nRead more in Fortune by Nick Lichtenberg. Article link in the first comment.",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-15T15:00:30.119Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/heykristopher_xbox-is-building-a-new-kind-of-flywheel-with-ugcPost-7513955395246161920-7a3g": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T13:06:47.708354+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "XBOX is building a new kind of flywheel with games at the center.\n\nThe company announced XP this morning (a clever title)âa new division headed by Kayleen Walters focused on creating more on-ramps for fans to its beloved IP through film & television, consumer products, live events, and strategic partnerships.\n\nHere are the four divisions:\n\n* XBOX PICTURES: Bringing our worlds and characters to new audiences through film, television, and other forms of linear storytelling. \n* XBOX PRODUCTS: Creating products that are authentic to the fandom that allow fans to celebrate and express the franchises they love. \n* XBOX PLACES: Bringing communities together through live events, immersive experiences, attractions, broadcasts, and destinations. \n* XBOX PARTNERSHIPS: Working with creators, brands, and communities to develop new experiences, sponsorships, and brand partnerships.\n\nThe moveâchampioned by Matthew Ball following an internal memo from Asha Sharmaâis both elegant and strategic. It adopts the best strategies from Disney and Nintendo, both of whom understand that content is king. Where Disneyâs flywheel was built strategically around film and television firs, Nintendoâs is game first.\n\nWith this move, XBOX is positioning itself to move beyond being a mere platform to owning its market position as both a publisher and steward of massive IP (from Minecraft to Halo and beyond).\n\nIâm excited to see where this leads.",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-08T13:36:08.988Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/moritzbaierlentz_game-studio-funding-is-back-gardens-interactive-share-7513608118791196673-sNWA": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T13:06:47.708354+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Game studio funding is back: Gardens Interactive has raised a $35M+ Series B, bringing total funding to over $70M before launching its flagship game.\n\nLed by Lightspeed, the round includes Sequoia Capital, Index Ventures, Accel, Eric Schmidt’s Innovation Endeavors, the Nintendo family (Yamauchi No.10), the ZeniMax Media family (James Altman), and the founders of Slack and OpenAI's Sora.\n\nBy any measure, but certainly in 2026, that's an extraordinary vote of confidence and tier-1 syndicate for a pre-launch studio. What inspires that conviction while it seems all venture dollars chase automation?\n\nA team creating a new genre around a simple and proven design principle: deepen human connections, and let the players be the fun.\n\nGardens calls it a “strandbox”: a social roleplaying world where chance encounters become adventures, players shape each other’s stories, and your actions leave something behind for whoever comes next.\n\nFrom serial game-of-the-year creators behind Journey and Sky, the team blends indie creativity and beautiful art with an ambitious AAA live-ops platform bet on how games can create significant and long-lasting emotional encounters.\n\nThis one is deeply personal. I love Stephen, 🔔Chris, and Lexie like brothers. After serving on Gardens’ board for the past three years, I’m rejoining as a personal investor and advisor, doubling down with my own capital and time. To continue an extraordinary development journey that already brought so many wonderful once-strangers together.\n\nI can’t wait for you all to play what they’re building.\n\nBloomberg exclusive by Cecilia D'Anastasio: https://lnkd.in/dYJ4Xj9C",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-07T14:36:12.326Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/paulcopplestone_today-supabase-is-announcing-150m-in-new-share-7511811435921072128-6ltf": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T13:06:47.708354+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Today, Supabase is announcing $150M in new funding, led by GIC, with CapitalG, IronArc Ventures, and Square Peg participating. We’re also welcoming Turso to Supabase.\n\nThe past year has been the fastest period of growth in Supabase’s history. We’re now adding more than 1M users and nearly 5M databases every month, and around 70% of new databases are being created by agents or AI-driven tools.\n\nAI is changing the economics of software creation. More people can build software, developers can build dramatically more of it, and agents are increasingly building alongside them.\n\nOur goal is to make Supabase the foundation for this agentic era. That means making it radically cheaper to start, while giving every application a clear path to scale.\nThat’s a big part of why we’re acquiring Turso.\n\nAs agents create more software, database demand will outpace the world’s current capacity. Turso has built an architecture that can handle vastly more small databases at a fraction of today’s cost. An agent can get an isolated database instantly, without requiring a dedicated machine for every workload.\n\nFor existing users, nothing changes. Supabase will continue building around Postgres, while Turso will continue its work on SQLite. Together, we’re creating something new that will bring the Supabase experience to every agent.\n\nThere’s a lot that brought our teams together: open source, developer experience, and a willingness to tackle hard infrastructure problems. We’re excited to welcome Glauber Costa , Pekka Enberg, and the entire Turso team to Supabase, with Glauber joining as Head of Agentic Services.\n\nThank you to GIC, CapitalG, IronArc, SquarePeg, and everyone who continues to support us. Most importantly, thank you to the Supabase community. You keep building faster than we expect, which means we have to keep doing the same.\n\nSri Muppidi has more on the news for the New York Times and we’ve shared more on the Supabase blog. Links in the comments.",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-02T15:36:49.683Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/todd-simmons-55364412_north-carolina-at-students-march-back-to-activity-7516656598392483840-6xHl": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T13:06:47.708354+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Clarification: On Thursday, Oct. 15, thousands of Aggie students took part in TWO major marches to downtown Greensboro:\n\n- The first was a March to the Polls, as previously described, which went from campus to the Union Square polling location downtown on the first day of early voting in North Carolina. Students marched back to campus after voting in protest of the Guilford County Elections Board's removal of their campus early voting polling location earlier this year.\n\n- The second was a March for Justice for Nolan Wells, the 18-year-old young man who tragically died July 4 under murky circumstances in the waters off Mississippi’s Horn Island after celebrating the Independence Day holiday. The march was organized by the A&T chapter of the NAACP, and a coalition of groups worked tirelessly to bring students together in solidarity for Nolan from across campus and the entire state. The march began at A&T’s February One monument, went downtown to the International Civil Rights Museum and returned to campus.\n\nIncredibly, thousands of Aggies took part in *both* marches, but in the video posted here, were returning from the second march, which concluded later. In both instances, outstanding civic leadership and participation were on full display from A&T students in the best tradition of Aggies, who have been leading in important community events since the university’s establishment in 1891. \n\nA&T continues to be America's largest HBCU, as well as its top-rated public HBCU in Forbes and US News & World Report.",
          "posted_at": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/todd-simmons-55364412_north-carolina-at-students-march-back-to-ugcPost-7516656540976795649-Vavy": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T13:06:47.708354+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Clarification: On Thursday, Oct. 15, thousands of Aggie students took part in TWO major marches to downtown Greensboro:\n\n- The first was a March to the Polls, as previously described, which went from campus to the Union Square polling location downtown on the first day of early voting in North Carolina. Students marched back to campus after voting in protest of the Guilford County Elections Board's removal of their campus early voting polling location earlier this year.\n\n- The second was a March for Justice for Nolan Wells, the 18-year-old young man who tragically died July 4 under murky circumstances in the waters off Mississippi’s Horn Island after celebrating the Independence Day holiday. The march was organized by the A&T chapter of the NAACP, and a coalition of groups worked tirelessly to bring students together in solidarity for Nolan from across campus and the entire state. The march began at A&T’s February One monument, went downtown to the International Civil Rights Museum and returned to campus.\n\nIncredibly, thousands of Aggies took part in *both* marches, but in the video posted here, were returning from the second march, which concluded later. In both instances, outstanding civic leadership and participation were on full display from A&T students in the best tradition of Aggies, who have been leading in important community events since the university’s establishment in 1891. \n\nA&T continues to be America's largest HBCU, as well as its top-rated public HBCU in Forbes and US News & World Report.",
          "posted_at": ""
        }
